{"seq": 96, "t": 65.23329629201908, "type": "memory_compact", "who": "Scarlett", "lines": 8, "so_far": "Tonight the gentlemen kept shouting over bourbon and war about giving Yankees the war they begged for. Rhett said coolly we have cotton and Yankees have cannon and foundries and Heaven favors larger battalions. An old man said war ain't glory it's fever and mud and boys dying crying for water. Ashley pulled me aside and offered the quiet library and I told Mr Butler to hush for spoiling everything.", "knows": ["Gerald is hot and eager to give Yankees war", "Stuart is sure one battle will make Yankees run", "old man has seen battle and knows it's not glory", "Rhett has seen their foundries and thinks cannon beats cotton"], "promised": ["Ashley promised me that walk to the quiet library"], "tried": ["told Ashley war talk bores me", "reminded Ashley he promised me the walk", "begged Ashley to look at me", "tried green to make my eyes his colour", "told Mr Butler to hush"]}
{"seq": 97, "t": 65.87303554202663, "type": "memory_compact", "who": "everyone here", "lines": 8, "so_far": "The men kept debating war as Gerald and Stuart clamored for a fight. An old veteran broke in to say war is fever and mud, not glory, and Rhett coolly backed him citing Yankee foundries. Ashley tried to draw Scarlett away to the quiet library while Scarlett pouted for his attention and told Rhett to hush.", "knows": ["Gerald is hot-headed and eager for war", "Stuart is hot and cocksure Yankees will run after one battle", "old man is a trembling veteran who knows war as screaming and mud", "Rhett is coolly polite, dryly amused, and defers to experience and numbers", "Scarlett is petulant, flirtatious, and desperate to be seen", "Ashley is soft, coaxing, and seeks quiet civility"], "promised": ["Ashley offered to fetch Scarlett more lemonade", "Ashley offered to walk with Scarlett toward the azaleas", "Scarlett asked Ashley to stay with her and look only at her", "Ashley invited Scarlett to the quiet library with door open for her"], "tried": ["warned cotton cannot beat Yankee cannon", "supported veteran and warned Yankee industry favors numbers", "placated gentlemen to stop shouting", "apologized and offered Scarlett lemonade", "invited Scarlett to walk to the azaleas", "spoke gravely that none should have to face war", "coaxed Scarlett to step away to the library", "boisterously demanded war on the Yankees", "bragged one battle will rout the Yankees", "countered glory talk with horror of dying boys"]}
